{"id": "EUVD-2026-102337", "enisaUuid": "02ef2b5a-190b-3114-a792-62b48a1cc30d", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE 2.5.0 through 2.9.0 contains an OS command injection vulnerability in openvpn.learn-address.sh that allows authenticated VPN clients to execute commands as the unbound user. Attackers can embed shell metacharacters in the certificate common name or username, which is interpolated unquoted into su -c strings, when DNS Resolver client registration is enabled.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:48:58", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-ovpn-learn-cn", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/sbin/openvpn.learn-address.sh#L57-L62", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-2.5.0-through-2.9.0-os-command-injection-via-openvpn-learn-address-sh"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111225", "GHSA-643j-4p8v-85c8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 6.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2a03afdb-e9e2-3132-a355-a30cbbfb83c8", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "2.5.0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "519291ce-34e7-3c17-8d47-9227b6b46d3e", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}